      "id": "001",
      "title": "Rust vs Python \u2014 the HTTP-direct floor",
      "status": "complete",
      "hypothesis": "A compiled language (Rust) posts a lower firing floor than Python for the HTTP-direct approach.",
      "method": "Ran approach_b_http in each language, 30 trials, against the local mock on loopback; scored release\u2192hit on the server's single monotonic clock.",
      "primary_metric": "p50_ms",
      "conclusion": "Rust posts the lower floor (~0.7 vs ~1.0 ms median), but both HTTP-direct langs cluster within ~1 ms \u2014 the approach dominates the language.",
      "decision": "Publish Rust as the record floor; keep Python for day-to-day iteration.",
